{
  "name": "basket_all_or_nothing",
  "asserts": "v3 E3: a neg-risk YES set is bought as one all-or-nothing basket (one position for the constraints); a leg without liquidity refuses the whole basket; the summary row sums the legs and settles with them",
  "derivation": [
    "Two neg-risk events, three YES tokens each (c1 and f2 are the catch-alls), every YES priced 0.30 at m0-m12; a1 and e2 resolve YES at m10 (closed m9), the rest NO. No fees, MARKET orders, TRADE_PRINT with unlimited participation and zero slippage.",
    "Basket rule NEGRISK_YES_SET, min_edge 0.02: margin = 1 - 0.90 - 0 fees - 0.03 ticks - 0.02 = 0.05 >= 0 -> both events signal at m0 (max_open_positions 2 counts a basket as one).",
    "m1: ev1 legs each print BUY 100 @ 0.30 -> fill 0.30, cost per unit 0.90; FIXED_CASH 30 -> floor(30 / 0.90, 2dp) = 33.33 units; three legs of 33.33 x 0.30 = 9.999 -> cash 100 - 29.997 = 70.003 (basket B1, seq 1-3).",
    "m1: ev2's f2y has no print -> NO_PRINTS on one leg -> the whole basket is UNEXECUTABLE_BASKET_LEG (BASKET_LEG_NO_PRINTS), seq 4, nothing bought.",
    "m2: ev1 is blocked by max_positions_per_event (its basket is one position); ev2 signals again and fills at m3 (f2y prints from m2): basket B3, seq 5-7, cash 40.006.",
    "m10 settlement: a1y and e2y pay 33.33 each, the other legs 0 -> cash 40.006 + 66.66 = 106.666. Each basket nets 33.33 - 29.997 = 3.333; summary rows (seq 8, 9) carry entry_price = sum of leg fills 0.90, shares = units, notional 29.997, exit_reason MARKET_RESOLVED once every leg settled."
  ],
